  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Dana, I checked your account and laptop. Your mailbox has plenty of room, your laptop is online with no warnings, and there are no unusual sign-in problems, so the issue looks local to the Outlook app on your laptop. Could you please do the following and let us know the result? First, open Outlook on the web (outlook.office.com) and see whether today's new mail is there. If it is, close Outlook completely and reopen it. Then check the Send / Receive tab and make sure Work Offline is turned off. If mail still doesn't arrive, restart the laptop. If it is still stuck after that, reply and we will rebuild your Outlook profile with you. If the web version also shows no new mail, tell us right away, since that would point to a larger problem.",
  "internal_note": "Checked lookup_user for user_id 1 (Dana Whitfield, CEO, VIP): account active, not blocked, no failed logins, must_change_password false, mailbox 8.9 GB of 50 GB (17.4%), so KB-010 does not apply. Checked device BL-LT-0101: online, last check-in 2026-10-11 03:23 UTC, 60.5% disk free, no warnings. Checked sign-in logs for last 14 days: 10 successful sign-ins, no failures, no MFA denials, all from New York on usual pattern, nothing anomalous. Outlook on the web status is not yet known; it was requested from the user per KB-009 step 1. Not yet done: user-side KB-009 fix steps (close/reopen, Work Offline check, restart, profile rebuild). Escalate to Tier 2 if OWA also shows no new mail or if other users report the same issue. Priority P3 per triage; given VIP status, a quick follow-up is advisable if the user responds that it is still failing.",
